{"parentUuid":"6ac974ff-e291-4307-8297-16be4ab82919","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\JaimeIbrahim","sessionId":"72d433ec-6330-42b7-944a-0b486d43bf82","version":"2.1.45","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"# JAIME IBRAHIM — Site Revisions for Claude Code\n## Priority: Jaime's Direct Revisions → Audit Improvements\n## Date: February 17, 2026\n\n> **Context:** jaimeibrahim.com is a Next.js 15 (App Router) portfolio deployed on Vercel.\n> Repo: `JosephOIbrahim/jaime-ibrahim-portfolio` on GitHub.\n> Pipeline: Claude Code → GitButler → GitHub → Vercel (auto-deploy on push).\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 0 — JAIME'S REVISIONS (DO FIRST)\n\nThese are direct client requests. Execute all four before moving to any audit batches.\n\n### 0A. Remove all dates from the project gallery\n\nThe project grid cards currently show years (2024, 2023, 2022) next to the category tag. Remove all year/date display from:\n\n- **Homepage featured work grid** — each card shows `{category}{year}` under the description. Remove the year.\n- **Work index page** (`/work`) — same treatment, remove year from all cards.\n- **Project detail pages** — if year appears in the project header/metadata, remove it there too.\n\n**Where to look:**\n- `lib/projects.ts` or `lib/data.ts` — the `PROJECTS` array likely has a `year` field. You can leave the data in place (don't delete from the data model), just stop rendering it.\n- The grid card component (likely in `components/` or inline in page files) — find where `year` or `project.year` is rendered and remove that JSX.\n- Check both the homepage (`app/page.tsx`) and work page (`app/work/page.tsx`) for any year rendering.\n\n**Verification:** Visit `/` and `/work` — no dates should appear on any project card.\n\n---\n\n### 0B. Delete the Thoughts section entirely\n\nThe site currently has a \"Thoughts\" nav link and a `/thoughts` page. Remove it completely:\n\n1. **Navigation** — Remove \"Thoughts\" from the nav links. The nav should only show: Work, About. Find the nav component (likely in `components/Nav.tsx` or `components/Navigation.tsx` or in the root layout) and delete the Thoughts link.\n2. **Page route** — Delete the entire `app/thoughts/` directory (page.tsx and any sub-routes like `app/thoughts/[slug]/`).\n3. **Data file** — If there's a `lib/thoughts.ts` or thoughts data in a shared data file, delete it or leave it (it won't be imported anywhere after removing the page).\n4. **Footer** — Check if \"Thoughts\" appears in the footer navigation. If so, remove it.\n5. **Sitemap** — If there's a `sitemap.ts` or `sitemap.xml` that includes `/thoughts`, remove that entry.\n\n**Verification:** \"Thoughts\" should not appear anywhere in the nav, footer, or sitemap. Visiting `/thoughts` should 404.\n\n---\n\n### 0C. Delete the Instagram link\n\nThe site footer and possibly the nav/header show both LinkedIn and Instagram social links. Remove Instagram:\n\n1. **Header/Nav** — Find where social links are rendered. Remove the Instagram link. Keep LinkedIn.\n2. **Footer** — Same — remove Instagram, keep LinkedIn.\n3. **About page** — If Instagram is linked on the about page, remove it.\n\n**Where to look:** Search the codebase for `instagram` (case-insensitive). Remove all references to the Instagram URL and link element.\n\n**Verification:** No Instagram link should appear anywhere on the site. LinkedIn remains.\n\n---\n\n### 0D. Update \"Brands I've Worked With\" list\n\nThe about page (and possibly the homepage or footer) shows a client/brands list. Replace the current list with Jaime's updated list:\n\n**NEW LIST (in this exact order):**\n1. Bloomberg\n2. GLG\n3. TIAA\n4. American Express\n5. Martha Stewart\n6. Bailard\n7. JC Flowers\n8. Johnson & Johnson\n9. Sony BMG\n10. Simon & Schuster\n11. Viacom\n12. Scholastic\n\n**Where to look:**\n- `app/about/page.tsx` — likely has a clients/brands section with an array of names.\n- `lib/data.ts` or `lib/projects.ts` — might have a `CLIENTS` or `BRANDS` array.\n- Search for any of the old brand names (Mastercard, JPMorgan, Deloitte, etc.) to find the exact location.\n\n**Replace the entire array** — don't append, replace. The old list was: Bloomberg, GLG, TIAA, Mastercard, JPMorgan Chase, Bank of America, Deloitte, EY, MetLife, Prudential, S&P Global, Moody's.\n\n**Verification:** Visit `/about` — the brands section should show exactly the 12 names above in order.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 1 — SEO METADATA (from site audit)\n\nAdd proper page-level metadata for every route. The root layout should already have a base `metadata` export — update each page to override with specific content.\n\n### Homepage (`app/page.tsx`)\n```typescript\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'Jaime Ibrahim | Brand Design Director',\n  description: 'Brand Design Director with 25+ years of experience in identity systems, visual storytelling, and strategic design for Bloomberg, GLG, TIAA, and more.',\n};\n```\n\n### Work page (`app/work/page.tsx`)\n```typescript\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'Work',\n  description: 'Selected projects spanning brand identity, systems design, event branding, and motion — 25 years of strategic visual design.',\n};\n```\n\n### About page (`app/about/page.tsx`)\n```typescript\nexport const metadata = {\n  title: 'About',\n  description: 'Jaime Ibrahim is a Brand Design Director based in New York City. Strategy before aesthetics. Systems over one-offs.',\n};\n```\n\n### Per-project pages (`app/work/[slug]/page.tsx`)\nAdd `generateMetadata` if not present:\n```typescript\nexport async function generateMetadata({ params }: { params: { slug: string } }) {\n  const project = getProjectBySlug(params.slug);\n  if (!project) return {};\n  return {\n    title: project.title,\n    description: project.desc,\n    openGraph: {\n      images: [`/images/${project.slug}/hero.jpg`],\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\n**Verification:** View page source on each route — `<title>` and `<meta name=\"description\">` should show the specified content.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 2 — 301 REDIRECTS FOR OLD SQUARESPACE URLS\n\nGoogle still has old Squarespace URLs indexed. Create `next.config.js` (or update existing) redirects so those URLs resolve instead of 404ing:\n\n```javascript\n// In next.config.js or next.config.mjs\nasync redirects() {\n  return [\n    // Old Squarespace portfolio slugs → new routes\n    { source: '/bank-visual-identity', destination: '/work/battlebank', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/glg-brand-identity', destination: '/work/glg-brand', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/glg-brand-video', destination: '/work/glg-video', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/glg-explainer-video', destination: '/work/glg-explainer', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/fintech-brand-identity', destination: '/work/liquidstock', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/event-brand-identity', destination: '/work/year-ahead', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/tiaa-branding', destination: '/work/tiaa', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/bloomberg-black', destination: '/work/bloomberg', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/employee-brand-identity', destination: '/work/employee-brand', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/opera-video', destination: '/work/opera', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/construction-wall', destination: '/work/construction', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/product-branding', destination: '/work/product-branding', permanent: true },\n    { source: '/visual-brand', destination: '/about', permanent: true },\n    // Catch old filtered views\n    { source: '/work-1', destination: '/work', permanent: true },\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n**Verification:** Visit `/bank-visual-identity` — should 301 redirect to `/work/battlebank`.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 3 — SITEMAP + ROBOTS + JSON-LD\n\n### Sitemap (`app/sitemap.ts`)\n```typescript\nimport { MetadataRoute } from 'next';\n\nexport default function sitemap(): MetadataRoute.Sitemap {\n  const projects = getAllProjects(); // import from your data file\n  \n  const projectUrls = projects.map((p) => ({\n    url: `https://jaimeibrahim.com/work/${p.slug}`,\n    lastModified: new Date(),\n    changeFrequency: 'monthly' as const,\n    priority: 0.8,\n  }));\n\n  return [\n    { url: 'https://jaimeibrahim.com', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'monthly', priority: 1.0 },\n    { url: 'https://jaimeibrahim.com/work', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'monthly', priority: 0.9 },\n    { url: 'https://jaimeibrahim.com/about', lastModified: new Date(), changeFrequency: 'monthly', priority: 0.7 },\n    ...projectUrls,\n  ];\n}\n```\n\n**NOTE:** Do NOT include `/thoughts` in the sitemap — that page is being deleted in Batch 0B.\n\n### Robots (`app/robots.ts`)\n```typescript\nimport { MetadataRoute } from 'next';\n\nexport default function robots(): MetadataRoute.Robots {\n  return {\n    rules: { userAgent: '*', allow: '/' },\n    sitemap: 'https://jaimeibrahim.com/sitemap.xml',\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### JSON-LD (in root layout or homepage)\nAdd a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` with Person schema:\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"Person\",\n  \"name\": \"Jaime Ibrahim\",\n  \"jobTitle\": \"Brand Design Director\",\n  \"url\": \"https://jaimeibrahim.com\",\n  \"sameAs\": [\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jaimeibrahim/\"],\n  \"knowsAbout\": [\"Brand Design\", \"Identity Systems\", \"Visual Design\", \"Creative Direction\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Verification:** Visit `/sitemap.xml` — should list all live pages (no `/thoughts`). Visit `/robots.txt` — should reference the sitemap.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 4 — IMAGE ALT TEXT\n\nEvery project hero image needs a descriptive alt tag. Find the Image components and update:\n\n| Project | Alt Text |\n|---------|----------|\n| battlebank | \"Battle Bank brand identity — logo, color palette, and mountain-inspired collateral\" |\n| glg-brand | \"GLG global rebrand — visual identity system across digital and print touchpoints\" |\n| glg-video | \"GLG brand manifesto video — motion graphics frames from global town hall presentation\" |\n| glg-explainer | \"GLG explainer video — animated frames showing how the insight network works\" |\n| liquidstock | \"Liquid Stock fintech brand identity — logo mark and California-inspired visual system\" |\n| year-ahead | \"The Year Ahead summit branding — event signage and collateral for Chicago business summit\" |\n| tiaa | \"TIAA enterprise rebrand — timeline installation, collateral, and retirement data project\" |\n| bloomberg | \"Bloomberg video installation — motion graphics for office digital displays\" |\n| employee-brand | \"Bloomberg employee brand — summer picnic series event identity\" |\n\n**Verification:** Inspect any project image in DevTools — `alt` attribute should contain a descriptive sentence, not empty or generic.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 5 — OG IMAGE GENERATION\n\nCreate `app/opengraph-image.tsx` using Next.js ImageResponse for auto-generated social share cards:\n\n```typescript\nimport { ImageResponse } from 'next/og';\n\nexport const runtime = 'edge';\nexport const alt = 'Jaime Ibrahim — Brand Design Director';\nexport const size = { width: 1200, height: 630 };\nexport const contentType = 'image/png';\n\nexport default async function Image() {\n  return new ImageResponse(\n    (\n      <div style={{\n        background: '#EEEEEC',\n        width: '100%',\n        height: '100%',\n        display: 'flex',\n        flexDirection: 'column',\n        justifyContent: 'center',\n        padding: '80px',\n        fontFamily: 'system-ui',\n      }}>\n        <div style={{ fontSize: 64, fontWeight: 400, color: '#1a1a1a', letterSpacing: '-0.01em' }}>\n          Jaime Ibrahim\n        </div>\n        <div style={{ fontSize: 24, color: '#767676', marginTop: 16, letterSpacing: '0.06em', textTransform: 'uppercase' }}>\n          Brand Design Director\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    ),\n    { ...size }\n  );\n}\n```\n\nAlso create per-project OG images at `app/work/[slug]/opengraph-image.tsx` that use the project title and category.\n\n**Verification:** Use https://cards-dev.twitter.com/validator or https://www.opengraph.xyz/ to check that jaimeibrahim.com generates a branded card.\n\n---\n\n## BATCH 6 — GA4 INTEGRATION\n\nInstall Google Analytics using the Next.js Script component. The user will provide the GA4 Measurement ID (format: `G-XXXXXXXXXX`).\n\n### Create `components/Analytics.tsx`\n```typescript\n'use client';\nimport Script from 'next/script';\n\nexport function Analytics() {\n  const GA_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID;\n  if (!GA_ID) return null;\n  \n  return (\n    <>\n      <Script src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA_ID}`} strategy=\"afterInteractive\" />\n      <Script id=\"ga4\" strategy=\"afterInteractive\">\n        {`window.dataLayer=window.dataLayer||[];function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments)}gtag('js',new Date());gtag('config','${GA_ID}');`}\n      </Script>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Add to root layout\nImport and render `<Analytics />` inside the `<body>` of `app/layout.tsx`.\n\n### Set environment variable\nIn Vercel dashboard → Project Settings → Environment Variables:\n- Key: `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID`\n- Value: `G-XXXXXXXXXX` (to be provided)\n\n**Verification:** After deploying with the env var set, check the browser Network tab for a request to `google-analytics.com` or `googletagmanager.com`.\n\n---\n\n## CANCELLED BATCHES\n\n~~**Batch 9 — Thoughts page seed content**~~ → CANCELLED. The Thoughts section is being deleted entirely (Batch 0B). Do not create any Thoughts-related content.\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTION ORDER\n\n```\nBatch 0A → 0B → 0C → 0D   (Jaime's revisions — do all four first, commit)\nBatch 1                     (SEO metadata — commit)\nBatch 2                     (Redirects — commit)\nBatch 3                     (Sitemap + robots + JSON-LD — commit)\nBatch 4                     (Alt text — commit)\nBatch 5                     (OG images — commit)\nBatch 6                     (GA4 — commit, needs Measurement ID)\n```\n\nEach batch should be a separate commit via GitButler for clean rollback if needed.\n\n---\n\n## CODEBASE ORIENTATION\n\n```\napp/\n├── layout.tsx          ← Root layout (nav, footer, fonts, metadata)\n├── page.tsx            ← Homepage (hero + featured grid)\n├── work/\n│   ├── page.tsx        ← Work index (all projects + filters)\n│   └── [slug]/\n│       └── page.tsx    ← Project detail\n├── about/\n│   └── page.tsx        ← About + brands list\n├── thoughts/           ← DELETE THIS ENTIRE DIRECTORY (Batch 0B)\n│   └── page.tsx\ncomponents/\n├── Nav.tsx (or Navigation.tsx)\n├── GridCard.tsx (or ProjectCard.tsx)\n├── Footer.tsx\nlib/\n├── projects.ts (or data.ts) ← Project data array + client list\npublic/\n├── images/             ← Project images organized by slug\n```\n\nFile names may vary — use `find` or `grep` to locate the exact files. The key data structures are:\n- A `PROJECTS` array with slug, title, category, desc, year fields\n- A `CLIENTS` or `BRANDS` array (for the about page)\n- Nav links defined either in the Nav component or root layout. think deeply\n\nCheck for consistency:\nhttps://thinkingmachines.ai/blog/defeating-nondeterminism-in-llm-inference/\n\nclaude --model opusplan --permission-mode acceptEdits"},"uuid":"251a5a4d-44cc-44f7-9280-2f43fcbb2765","timestamp":"2026-02-18T00:56:46.281Z","thinkingMetadata":{"maxThinkingTokens":31999},"todos":[],"permissionMode":"default"}
